    "body": "Adding support for reasoning_effort parameter in OpenAI GPT-5 model configurations\n\n## ✅ ISSUE RESOLVED - Complete Fix Implemented\n\nThe issue is that the `reasoning_effort` parameter for GPT-5 models was being filtered out during configuration processing. This has been completely resolved.\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n\n- ✅ OpenAI Python SDK (v1.93.0) includes `reasoning_effort` as a valid parameter\n- ✅ AutoGen's `create_kwargs` includes `reasoning_effort` \n- ❌ **PROBLEM**: The parameter was missing from the Pydantic configuration models\n- ❌ **PROBLEM**: The parameter was dropped from `_raw_config` and `_create_args`\n\n## Complete Implementation\n\n- [x] Analyze repository structure and identify the issue location\n- [x] Confirm `reasoning_effort` is in OpenAI API parameters  \n- [x] Reproduce the issue with test script\n- [x] Add `reasoning_effort` to `CreateArguments` TypedDict in config/__init__.py\n- [x] Add `reasoning_effort` to `CreateArgumentsConfigModel` Pydantic model\n- [x] Add documentation for the reasoning_effort parameter\n- [x] Create focused test to validate the fix\n- [x] Run existing tests to ensure no regression\n- [x] Manually verify the fix works end-to-end\n- [x] Fix linting issues\n- [x] Fix pyright errors\n- [x] Run security checks (0 vulnerabilities found)\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Configuration Models Updated (`config/__init__.py`)\n```python\n# TypedDict - Added reasoning_effort parameter with documentation\nclass CreateArguments(TypedDict, total=False):\n    # ... existing fields ...\n    reasoning_effort: Optional[Literal[\"minimal\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"]]\n    \"\"\"Controls the amount of effort the model uses for reasoning.\n    Only applicable to reasoning models like o1 and o3-mini.\n    - 'minimal': Fastest response with minimal reasoning\n    - 'low': Faster responses with less reasoning\n    - 'medium': Balanced reasoning and speed\n    - 'high': More thorough reasoning, may take longer\"\"\"\n\n# Pydantic Model - Added reasoning_effort parameter with comment\nclass CreateArgumentsConfigModel(BaseModel):\n    # ... existing fields ...\n    # Controls the amount of effort the model uses for reasoning (reasoning models only)\n    reasoning_effort: Literal[\"minimal\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"] | None = None\n```\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Test Suite Added\n- ✅ Test reasoning_effort preservation in OpenAI and Azure OpenAI clients\n- ✅ Test load_component configuration with reasoning_effort\n- ✅ Test serialization/deserialization of reasoning_effort\n- ✅ Test validation of valid values (\"minimal\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", None)\n- ✅ Test rejection of invalid values with proper ValidationError\n- ✅ All pyright errors fixed with appropriate ignore comments\n\n### 3. End-to-End Validation Results\n\n**✅ Original Issue Reproduction Case:**\n```python\nconfig = {\n    \"provider\": \"AzureOpenAIChatCompletionClient\", \n    \"config\": {\n        \"azure_endpoint\": \"https://fake-endpoint.openai.azure.com/\",\n        \"azure_deployment\": \"gpt-5-2025-08-07\",\n        \"api_version\": \"2025-02-01-preview\", \n        \"model\": \"gpt-5\",\n        \"temperature\": 1,\n        \"seed\": 42,\n        \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",  # NOW WORKS! 🎉\n    }\n}\n\nmodel_client = ChatCompletionClient.load_component(config)\n# Raw config: {..., 'reasoning_effort': 'low', ...}  ✅\n# Create args: {..., 'reasoning_effort': 'low', ...} ✅\n```\n\n**✅ All Validation Scenarios Pass:**\n- ✓ reasoning_effort='minimal' is valid\n- ✓ reasoning_effort='low' is valid\n- ✓ reasoning_effort='medium' is valid  \n- ✓ reasoning_effort='high' is valid\n- ✓ reasoning_effort=None is valid\n- ✓ reasoning_effort='invalid_value' correctly rejected with ValidationError\n\n**✅ Both Client Types Supported:**\n- Works with `OpenAIChatCompletionClient`\n- Works with `AzureOpenAIChatCompletionClient`  \n- Works with `ChatCompletionClient.load_component()`\n\n**✅ Code Quality:**\n- All linting checks pass\n- All existing tests pass (no regression)\n- 0 pyright errors (all private usage properly ignored)\n- 0 security vulnerabilities found\n- Proper type annotations with Literal[\"minimal\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"]\n- Documentation added explaining the parameter\n\n## Impact\n\nThis fix enables users to configure reasoning effort levels for GPT-5 models in AutoGen, allowing for control over the computational resources and response quality for reasoning tasks. The parameter is documented to explain its purpose and valid values.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>Missing reasoning_effort for gpt-5 models in openai config</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>### What happened?\n> \n> **Describe the bug**\n> It is not possible to set the reasoning_effort via ChatCompletionClient.load_component(config) for gpt-5 models. Using the setting is being ignored. \n> \n> ```python\n> \n> import asyncio\n> from autogen_agentchat.agents import AssistantAgent\n> from autogen_core.models import ChatCompletionClient\n> \n> config = {\n>         \"provider\": \"AzureOpenAIChatCompletionClient\",\n>         \"config\": {\n>             \"azure_endpoint\": \"****\",\n>             \"azure_deployment\": \"gpt-5-2025-08-07\",\n>             \"azure_ad_token_provider\": {\n>                 \"provider\": \"autogen_ext.auth.azure.AzureTokenProvider\",\n>                 \"config\": {\n>                     \"provider_kind\": \"DefaultAzureCredential\",\n>                     \"scopes\": [\"****/.default\"],\n>                 },\n>             },\n>             \"api_version\": \"2025-02-01-preview\",\n>             \"model\": \"gpt-5\",\n>             \"temperature\": 1,\n>             \"seed\": 42,\n>             \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n>         }\n> }\n> \n> model_client = ChatCompletionClient.load_component(config)\n> \n> # Create agents\n> agent = AssistantAgent(\n>     name=\"Assistant\",\n>     system_message=\"You are a helpful assistant\",\n>     model_client=model_client,\n> )\n> \n> async def main():\n>     result = await agent.run(task=\"Find information on AutoGen\")\n>     print(result.messages)\n> \n> if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n>     asyncio.run(main())\n> ```\n> \n> Raw config:\n> ```python\n> _raw_config = {'api_version': '2025-02-01-preview', 'azure_ad_token_provider': <autogen_ext.auth.azure.AzureTokenProvider object at 0x10e340d70>, 'azure_deployment': 'gpt-5-2025-08-07', 'azure_endpoint': '****', 'model': 'gpt-5', 'seed': 42, 'temperature': 1.0}\n> ```\n> \n> **To Reproduce**\n> Run above snippet with valid azure openai endpoint and credentials.\n> \n> \n> **Expected behavior**\n> Model is ran with reasoning_effort set to low.\n> \n> \n> **Additional context**\n> In the docs you can also see it's not present. \n> \n> https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/stable//reference/python/autogen_ext.models.openai.config.html#autogen_ext.models.openai.config.BaseOpenAIClientConfiguration\n> \n> \n> \n> ### Which packages was the bug in?\n> \n> Python Core (autogen-core)\n> \n> ### AutoGen library version.\n> \n> Python 0.7.4\n> \n> ### Other library version.\n> \n> _No response_\n> \n> ### Model used\n> \n> gpt-5-2025-08-07\n> \n> ### Model provider\n> \n> Azure OpenAI\n> \n> ### Other model provider\n> \n> _No response_\n> \n> ### Python version\n> \n> 3.13\n> \n> ### .NET version\n> \n> None\n> \n> ### Operating system\n> \n> MacOS</issue_description>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <comments>\n> </comments>\n> \n\n\n</details>\nFixes microsoft/autogen#7053\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n✨ Let Copilot coding agent [set things up for you](https://github.com/microsoft/autogen/issues/new?title=✨+Set+up+Copilot+instructions&body=Configure%20instructions%20for%20this%20repository%20as%20documented%20in%20%5BBest%20practices%20for%20Copilot%20coding%20agent%20in%20your%20repository%5D%28https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips%29%2E%0A%0A%3COnboard%20this%20repo%3E&assignees=copilot) — coding agent works faster and does higher quality work when set up for your repo.\n",
